Reaching fidelity $0.90$ takes
about $1.2\times10^4$ queries on AG-News, $5.0\times10^4$ on DBpedia and
$2.0\times10^5$ on Banking77. The head has $\Cc d$ parameters, and in each case fidelity $0.90$ costs
between three and five times that number of queries. A deployment can therefore set its
allowance from $\Cc$ and $d$ without repeating this experiment. \trsee{sec:experiments} gives the extraction study in full.
