\emph{Fidelity} is the rate at which a copy agrees with the served
model. Reaching fidelity $0.90$ takes
about $1.2\times10^4$ queries on AG-News, $5.0\times10^4$ on DBpedia and
$2.0\times10^5$ on Banking77. The head has $\Cc d$ parameters, where $d$ is the
feature dimension, and in each case fidelity $0.90$ costs
between three and five times that number of queries. A deployment can therefore set its
allowance from $\Cc$ and $d$ without repeating this experiment.   gives the extraction study in full.
