# 2026-08-29. Report view of a paragraph changed today when the reported
# latency moved to the specified design. Same change as the submission view,
# with the report's extra sentences.
\paragraph{The argmax} The argmax is the one operation in the protocol that is
not shallow. Evaluated as a sequential fold of $\Cc-1$ comparisons it takes about
$16$\,s per comparison, which is roughly twenty-six minutes at a hundred classes.
Packing the logits into one ciphertext and reducing them by a tournament lowers the
number of sequential comparisons from $\Cc-1$ to $\lceil\log_2\Cc\rceil$ and
brings the same computation to under two minutes at a hundred classes, a
fourteenfold reduction. Both figures restore levels by collective refresh, so the
ratio measures the reduction and not the mechanism. Because
homomorphic evaluation under a collectively generated key is identical to
evaluation under a single key, single-key results carry over, and GPU
implementations of the same reduction report a full-vocabulary argmax in well under
a second~\cite{zhang2025nexus}.
