\paragraph{Which mechanism produced the reported latency} Every latency
above is the specified design, in which the server restores levels on its own
under the collectively generated keys.   sets it beside the
collective refresh, which is about thirteen times faster and costs a share from
every client at every restoration. We report the specified design because it is
the one the method describes, and because a protocol that moved gigabytes to the
clients on every query would not be servable at the federation sizes this paper
considers. Every figure is single-core, and the restoration is the part that
would gain most from threads.
