The circuit is bootstrap-bound, so one number sets the accelerated figure.
Level restoration is $97$ per cent of a query and costs $23.1$\,s on one core at
every label-space size. We measure one restoration under Phantom on an NVIDIA
H100 at $2.28$\,s, at the ring degree $2^{16}$ the protocol restores at, a factor
of ten. Substituting it, and leaving the local evaluation on the processor, gives
$48.9$\,s at four classes, $100.1$\,s at fourteen and $176.6$\,s at a hundred,
against the $400.8$\,s and $1468.3$\,s of  . The local evaluation,
which we did not port, is then the larger half of a query above four classes.
